+## OAuth2 Provider Options
+
+InvenTree acts as an OAuth2 / OpenID Connect provider using [django-oauth-toolkit](https://django-oauth-toolkit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/settings.html). Additional options for the toolkit (for example token lifetimes, `DCR_ENABLED`, `CIMD_ENABLED` or `ALLOW_LOCALHOST_LOOPBACK`) can be supplied as a dictionary, which is merged into the `OAUTH2_PROVIDER` setting. Keys provided here take precedence over the InvenTree defaults (`SCOPES`, `OIDC_ENABLED`, `OIDC_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY`, `PKCE_REQUIRED`), so override those with care.
+
+The environment variable must contain a valid JSON object, e.g. `INVENTREE_OAUTH2_PROVIDER='{"ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_SECONDS": 3600}'`. The names (not the values) of overridden keys are written to the log at startup.
+
+{{ configtable() }}
+{{ configsetting("INVENTREE_OAUTH2_PROVIDER") }} Dictionary of django-oauth-toolkit options |
+
 ## Database Options
 
 InvenTree provides support for multiple database backends - any backend supported natively by Django can be used.
diff --git a/src/backend/InvenTree/InvenTree/config.py b/src/backend/InvenTree/InvenTree/config.py
index facd3b987..94ee515db 100644
--- a/src/backend/InvenTree/InvenTree/config.py
+++ b/src/backend/InvenTree/InvenTree/config.py
@@ -252,6 +252,28 @@ def do_typecast(value, type, var_name=None):
     return value
 
 
+def merge_oauth2_provider_settings(base: dict, overrides: Optional[dict]) -> dict:
+    """Merge user-supplied django-oauth-toolkit options into the core defaults.
+
+    Arguments:
+        base: The OAUTH2_PROVIDER dict defined by InvenTree
+        overrides: User-supplied options (from config.yaml or the environment)
+
+    Returns:
+        A new dict; keys in 'overrides' replace those in 'base'.
+        Only the names of overridden keys are logged, never the values.
+    """
+    result = dict(base)
+
+    if overrides and isinstance(overrides, dict):
+        logger.info(
+            'Overriding OAUTH2_PROVIDER settings: %s', ', '.join(sorted(overrides))
+        )
+        result.update(overrides)
+
+    return result
+
+
 def get_config_value(config_key: str) -> Optional[Any]:
     """Helper function to retrieve a configuration value from the config file."""
     cfg_data = load_config_data()
